MVP mode engaged. Here’s a lean, bootable Minetest mod that does exactly the stripped-down loop:

One world, rectangular plots you define in-game.

Land ownership is tracked locally (you’ll swap to your DB later; hooks included).

AIs (“Bothaviors”) spawn, wander for novelty, and teleport when persuaded or bored.

Players can talk to AIs to lure them to their plot: !talk <ai_name> <message>.

Point accrual = seconds an AI spends on a plot owned by someone and not walled (tax paid).

Taxes: every new player gets 1000 ENERGY. Pay 100 ENERGY to activate your plot’s 24 hours of access; after that, glass walls auto-appear until you pay again.

Everything else (NFTs, moons, lasers, multi-tokens) is happily ignored. You get clean, commented, working code you can run today and later swap the internals to your external DB.

Install quickstart

Install Minetest 5.7+

Create a world and drop this folder into worldmods/:

bothavior_simple/
